    text: "The trainer chat in Workout Director sends each message through the backend to a text model. Most of the work is in what goes into that request and what is allowed to come back.\n\nThe request is built in a fixed order. First the instructions, then what rarely changes about the person: their profile, the facts the trainer has been told to remember, and a summary of older chat. Then the last 24 messages, then what changes every turn: the time, today's plan, the last seven days of training and any food logged today.\n\nThat order follows the provider's prompt cache. The parts that rarely change stay at the front, so they can be reused from one message to the next.\n\nOnce a chat has 36 messages since the last summary, everything but the newest 24 is folded into a running summary, which the model is asked to keep to eight short lines.\n\nThe model has to reply in one JSON shape: one to three replies, up to six memory changes, and any food or training the person reported. A memory change is a remember or a forget, and a remember can replace an older fact by its id. The prompt says to keep only lasting facts the person stated, not moods or guesses.\n\nEach message carries a client id. If a dropped connection makes the phone send the same one twice, the backend returns the stored reply instead of calling the model again.",
